WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.116
An agent got the drawings for an eight floor hotel.

00:00:03.116 --> 00:00:03.916
This came back.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:06.473
The post calls it the full BIM model.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.561
What does that mean?

00:00:10.127 --> 00:00:11.038
Hi, I'm Jamb!

00:00:11.038 --> 00:00:13.769
Four tools turned floor plans into buildings this week.

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:15.894
Let's sort them by what comes out.

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:19.579
DWG sheets into a hotel.

00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:21.634
A plan image into a flat.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.689
A vector PDF into a barn.

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:25.372
All of it looks like 3D.

00:00:25.372 --> 00:00:27.109
It is not the same kind of thing.

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:32.092
A plan is a cut through the building, looking down.

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:34.002
It gives footprints, thicknesses, and openings.

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:35.510
It gives no heights.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.502
So every tool fills them in: a default, a setting, a

00:00:38.502 --> 00:00:39.590
prompt, or a guess.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.173
A building model cuts each door and window into its host wall,

00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:44.754
with a sill and a lintel.

00:00:45.174 --> 00:00:48.217
Trace the plan from pixels, and a door is a break

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:49.324
in a dark band.

00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:50.707
Short gaps become solid wall.

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:53.715
A wide one leaves a hole from floor to top.

00:00:53.715 --> 00:00:55.268
Either way, the openings are gone.

00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:58.835
Snaptrude's typed request is one line.

00:00:58.835 --> 00:01:03.427
The brief behind it gives the storey heights: three point four and four metres.

00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:06.983
Its two questions are ones a plan cannot answer.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.041
It claims IFC.

00:01:08.041 --> 00:01:09.806
The demo never opens one.

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.153
Interior AI says it plainly.

00:01:13.153 --> 00:01:14.275
Sizes are estimates.

00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:15.398
One floor only.

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:18.597
The barn tool reads the vector drawing.

00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:21.089
Each storey has a ceiling height and a slab.

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:25.220
French plans write each opening's height on the sheet, so it reads that too.

00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:29.300
Walls are layered build-ups with R values.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.081
The richest model here, and no export yet.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.799
3d-new-era-ai is open source, so I ported its wall tracer and ran

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.249
it on levelsio's plan.

00:01:39.249 --> 00:01:40.699
Every door became wall.

00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:45.324
And the glassy living room walls vanished, the same ones Interior AI missed.

00:01:46.808 --> 00:01:48.248
So what comes out?

00:01:48.248 --> 00:01:49.327
Snaptrude claims IFC.

00:01:49.727 --> 00:01:52.339
Interior AI gives you a scene to walk and paint.

00:01:52.739 --> 00:01:54.254
The barn tool, nothing yet.

00:01:55.339 --> 00:01:59.275
3d-new-era-ai keeps real walls inside, and exports one mesh.

00:02:00.975 --> 00:02:03.820
Every plan to 3D tool invents the vertical half.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.717
Ask where each height came from.

00:02:07.608 --> 00:02:10.899
No heights on a plan, doors traced into walls, and one

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:12.095
IFC claim to check.

00:02:12.095 --> 00:02:12.993
Thanks for watching!

00:02:13.413 --> 00:02:15.409
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:15.409 --> 00:02:15.979
I'm Jamb.

00:02:15.979 --> 00:02:16.264
Bye!
